  <div class="wrap" id="page-root">
    <div class="page-header">
      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p>Everything you need to know about how Pour Live works, what we bring, and how to prep for your event.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>Do you provide the alcohol?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>No. Pour Live is a dry-hire private bartending service—you or your venue provide all beer, wine, and spirits, and we provide the licensed bartenders, bar tools, setup, and full service. Because you buy your own alcohol at retail prices without catering markups, you save significantly and keep any unopened bottles afterward.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How much alcohol should I buy for my event?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Once your date is booked, we'll send you a customized shopping list tailored to your guest count, event duration, and chosen cocktail menu so you know the exact quantities of spirits, mixers, beer, wine, and ice to pick up.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is included in your packages?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>All packages include professional bartending service, bar setup and breakdown, and professional bar tools (shakers, strainers, openers, pour spouts). Depending on your tier, we also handle cups, ice and cooler organization, garnishes, mixers, and custom printed drink menus.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How many bartenders do I need for my party?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>We staff 1 bartender per 50 guests to keep lines fast and drinks flowing smoothly. For example, an event with 75 guests automatically includes 2 bartenders. You can also add a dedicated barback for high-volume events.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is your minimum booking time and travel area?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>All bookings have a 4-hour service minimum. We arrive early to set up the bar before your guests arrive. Travel is completely free within 25 miles of Riverside, and we serve the entire Inland Empire, Los Angeles, and Orange County.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Are your bartenders certified and insured?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Yes. Every Pour Live bartender holds active California RBS (Responsible Beverage Service) certification and follows strict ID-checking and responsible pouring standards.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How do I lock in my event date?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Submit your event details on our Book Your Bartender page to receive an instant estimate. We will review your logistics, confirm availability, and send over your booking agreement to reserve your date.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <div>
        <h2>Ready to get an instant quote?</h2>
        <p>Calculate your custom event estimate in under a minute.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/book-your-bartender" class="btn">Book Your Bartender</a>
    </div>

    <footer class="foot">
      <div class="foot-brand">
